    {
      "title": "v3 architecture · Representing network flows",
      "notes": "https://arxiv.org/html/2605.13986v1 Figure 5, Section 2.1. Original figure on the left, without a visible caption per user instruction. Steps 1–3 follow cell embedding, column-wise feature embedding, and row-wise feature aggregation. The labelled context is external input; the diagram does not depict IDS weight fine-tuning.",
      "items": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.33,
          "w": 12.1,
          "h": 0.57,
          "text": "v3 architecture · Representing network flows",
          "size": 30,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "00306C"
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "x": 0.62,
          "y": 1.08,
          "w": 3.95,
          "h": 5.88,
          "path": "/home/user/Desktop/imbalcic/docs/slides/_support/qa/kor/1015_labmeeting_qa/v3_architecture_page.png",
          "crop": [
            0.2,
            0.082,
            0.19,
            0.285
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "x": 4.98,
          "y": 1.4,
          "w": 7.73,
          "h": 0.45,
          "text": "1  Encode values · Cell embedding",
          "size": 22,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "007BC6"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "x": 5.33,
          "y": 2.08,
          "w": 7.25,
          "h": 0.87,
          "text": "Convert each value, such as packet length, into a vector\nInclude an indicator for missing values",
          "size": 20,
          "bold": false,
          "color": "20262E"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "x": 4.98,
          "y": 3.1399999999999997,
          "w": 7.73,
          "h": 0.45,
          "text": "2  Summarize columns · Feature embedding",
          "size": 22,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "007BC6"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "x": 5.33,
          "y": 3.82,
          "w": 7.25,
          "h": 0.87,
          "text": "Summarize each feature across multiple flows\nUse the labels supplied with the context",
          "size": 20,
          "bold": false,
          "color": "20262E"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "x": 4.98,
          "y": 4.88,
          "w": 7.73,
          "h": 0.45,
          "text": "3  Combine features · Feature aggregation",
          "size": 22,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "007BC6"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "x": 5.33,
          "y": 5.56,
          "w": 7.25,
          "h": 0.87,
          "text": "Combine a flow’s features into one representation\nPrepare it for comparison with other flows",
          "size": 20,
          "bold": false,
          "color": "20262E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "v3 architecture · Context-based prediction",
      "notes": "https://arxiv.org/html/2605.13986v1 Sections 2.2 and 2.4.2. The decoder averages one-hot context labels with learned attention weights. Cached prediction can reuse prepared context states; changing context may require recomputation. No claim that a context update is free, or universally faster than XGBoost refitting.",
      "items": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.33,
          "w": 12.1,
          "h": 0.57,
          "text": "v3 architecture · Context-based prediction",
          "size": 30,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "00306C"
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "x": 0.62,
          "y": 1.08,
          "w": 3.95,
          "h": 5.88,
          "path": "/home/user/Desktop/imbalcic/docs/slides/_support/qa/kor/1015_labmeeting_qa/v3_architecture_page.png",
          "crop": [
